{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a93b7a8dc732b51f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n3\ttitle: Select Feast deployment topology for productization\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: RHOAI Feature Store\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Select Feast deployment topology for productization\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the strategy's open question: which Feast deployment topology Red Hat\n30\tproductizes first — the operator-based deployment or the standalone server per\n31\tproject. Upstream Feast supports both; supportability, deployment artifact shape,\n32\tendpoint granularity, and the Platform Operator integration all differ. This\n33\tinvestigation produces the decision that determines the structure of the Feature\n34\tStore deployment and enablement work.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Analyze both supported upstream topologies (operator-based deployment; standalone\n39\t  server per project) for supportability, lifecycle management, upgrade path, and\n40\t  fit with platform managed-component enablement.\n41\t- Determine the endpoint model each topology produces (per-project endpoints vs.\n42\t  shared/central endpoints) and its implications for Dashboard link-out.\n43\t- Assess upstream maturity and maintenance burden of each option (operator\n44\t  maturity, release cadence, OpenShift compatibility).\n45\t- Recommend one topology to productize first, with the decision recorded and\n46\t  accepted by stakeholders, and identify which conditional branch of downstream\n47\t  work it activates.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- A decision document compares both topologies against explicit supportability\n52\t  criteria and records a single recommended topology.\n53\t- The recommendation states the endpoint granularity the chosen topology exposes\n54\t  per project, so Dashboard integration scope can be finalized.\n55\t- The decision is reviewed and accepted by the Feature Store stakeholders and the\n56\t  teams owning Platform Operator and Dashboard integration.\n57\t- Downstream deployment, enablement, and Dashboard integration scope is confirmed\n58\t  against the selected topology.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-1 (P0): gates the deployment productization and Platform Operator enablement\n63\t  work that delivers operator-based enablement with productized images.\n64\t- HLR-3 (P1): the chosen topology determines the endpoint model the Dashboard\n65\t  links to.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8488f4023ed4cd1b","agent_id":"a267e8dc1d2a50c9c","session_id":"385beecc-1fc6-46ba-a853-90e78b018c5f","uuid":"f5fca11a-32ad-4455-8b8c-6d2cabe781bc","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:11:02.291Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a93b7a8dc732b51f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
