{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2e2263558fb7f3c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n3\tepic_count: 7\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9006 (Feature Store as a supported RHOAI component)\n10\t\n11\t## Triage\n12\t\n13\tNot triaged. The strategy spans four components (Feature Store, Platform Operator,\n14\tNotebooks via workbench images, Dashboard, Documentation), multiple teams, HLRs at\n15\tthree priority levels, and architecturally distinct work streams (repo/build\n16\tonboarding, deployment productization, operator enablement, workbench image content,\n17\tDashboard UI, documentation). Step 0 escape conditions for below-threshold are met on\n18\twork streams alone; full decomposition follows.\n19\t\n20\t## Step 1 — Strategy Structure\n21\t\n22\tSections available: Problem Statement, High-Level Requirements (HLR-1..HLR-4 with\n23\tpriorities), Affected Components (list, no change/owner detail), Out of Scope, Open\n24\tQuestions (1).\n25\t\n26\tMissing sections (health warnings, see below): Impacted Teams table, Dependencies\n27\ttable, Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then), Non-Functional Requirements, Staff\n28\tEngineer Input. Teams were inferred from component ownership; the Dashboard team is\n29\tconfirmed by architecture context (`architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`, owning team\n30\tRHOAI Dashboard). No Staff Engineer Input exists, so no overrides were logged.\n31\t\n32\t## Step 2 — Component Graph\n33\t\n34\t| Strategy component | Canonical component (.context/rhai-components.txt) | In platform? | Active/Passive | Team | Epics |\n35\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n36\t| Feature Store | Feature Store | No — new component (no architecture context file) | Active | RHOAI Feature Store (inferred) | Investigation + onboarding chain + deployment implementation (branch) |\n37\t| Platform Operator | Platform Operator | Yes (existing managed-component framework per strategy: \"like any other managed component\") | Active | RHOAI Platform Operator (inferred) | Enablement implementation (branch) |\n38\t| Workbench images (HLR-2) | Notebooks | Yes (existing supported workbench images per HLR-2) | Active | RHOAI Notebooks (inferred) | SDK workbench-image implementation |\n39\t| Dashboard | Dashboard | Yes — architecture context file exists | Active | RHOAI Dashboard | Dashboard integration implementation |\n40\t| Documentation | Documentation | n/a | Active | RHOAI Documentation (inferred) | docs-authoring epic |\n41\t\n42\tComponent name mappings are exact matches to the canonical list; no non-obvious\n43\tmappings were needed. The strategy's \"workbench image\" scope maps to the canonical\n44\t**Notebooks** component.\n45\t\n46\t## Step 3 — Investigation Epics\n47\t\n48\tUnknowns scan (open questions table, risks, assumptions, pending reviews, conditional\n49\tADRs): the strategy contains exactly one open question — **which Feast deployment\n50\ttopology to productize first (operator-based deployment vs. standalone server per\n51\tproject)**.\n52\t\n53\t- Does the answer change which downstream epics exist or what they do? **Yes.** It\n54\t  determines what deployment artifacts are productized (operator + CRDs vs.\n55\t  per-project server manifests), how the Platform Operator enables the component,\n56\t  and the endpoint granularity the Dashboard links to (per-project vs. central).\n57\t  → **Investigation epic E001**, gating the deployment productization, operator\n58\t  enablement, and Dashboard integration.\n59\t- Bounded outcomes (2) → conditional decomposition branches A and B (see below).\n60\t\n61\tNo other unknowns qualify. Remaining unclear passages (which workbench image\n62\tvariant, image tagging, doc toolchain details) are implementation details captured\n63\tas acceptance criteria, not investigations.\n64\t\n65\t## Epic List (main plan)\n66\t\n67\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n68\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n69\t| E001 | Select Feast deployment topology for productization | Investigation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n70\t| E002 | Create midstream Feast repository under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n71\t| E003 | License validation for Feast and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n72\t| E004 | Onboard Feast midstream repository to Konflux | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n73\t| E005 | Preinstall Feast SDK in a supported workbench image | Implementation | RHOAI Notebooks | P1 |\n74\t| E006 | Dashboard: Feature Store enabled-component display and endpoint links | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n75\t| E007 | Feature Store product documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n76\t\n77\t### Branch epics (conditional, not standalone Jira issues)\n78\t\n79\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n80\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n81\t| BRANCH-A-E005 | Productize operator-based Feast deployment | Implementation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n82\t| BRANCH-A-E006 | Enable Feature Store via Platform Operator (operator topology) | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n83\t| BRANCH-B-E005 | Productize standalone per-project Feast server deployment | Implementation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n84\t| BRANCH-B-E006 | Enable Feature Store via Platform Operator (standalone topology) | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n85\t\n86\tBranch A = operator-based topology selected; Branch B = standalone server per\n87\tproject selected. Exactly one branch is activated by E001's outcome; the other is\n88\tdropped.\n89\t\n90\t## Dependency DAG (main plan)\n91\t\n92\t```mermaid\n93\tgraph TD\n94\t    E001[E001 Topology investigation] --> E006[E006 Dashboard integration]\n95\t    E002[E002 repo-onboarding] --> E004[E004 konflux-onboarding]\n96\t    E003[E003 license-validation] --> E005[E005 Feast SDK workbench image]\n97\t    E001 --> E007[E007 docs-authoring]\n98\t    E002 --> E007\n99\t    E003 --> E007\n100\t    E004 --> E007\n101\t    E005 --> E007\n102\t    E006 --> E007\n103\t```\n104\t\n105\t### Branch DAGs\n106\t\n107\t```mermaid\n108\tgraph TD\n109\t    E001[E001 investigation] --> A5[BRANCH-A-E005 operator deployment]\n110\t    E002[E002 repo-onboarding] --> A5\n111\t    E003[E003 license-validation] --> A5\n112\t    E001 --> A6[BRANCH-A-E006 operator enablement]\n113\t    E003 --> A6\n114\t    A5 --> A6\n115\t```\n116\t\n117\t```mermaid\n118\tgraph TD\n119\t    E001[E001 investigation] --> B5[BRANCH-B-E005 standalone server]\n120\t    E002[E002 repo-onboarding] --> B5\n121\t    E003[E003 license-validation] --> B5\n122\t    E001 --> B6[BRANCH-B-E006 operator enablement]\n123\t    E003 --> B6\n124\t    B5 --> B6\n125\t```\n126\t\n127\t## DAG Justification\n128\t\n129\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n130\t|---|---|---|\n131\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 5 | Konflux onboarding needs the repository to exist. |\n132\t| E002 → BRANCH-A/B-E005 | Rule 6 | Deployment productization is general implementation in the onboarded Feast repo; code needs the repo. |\n133\t| (E003 ∥ E002) | Rule 7 | License scanning and repo creation have independent inputs; both are roots. |\n134\t| (E004 ∥ implementations) | Rule 10 | Konflux onboarding runs parallel to general implementation; coupling enforced by \"build pipeline green\" ACs (Rule 25), never by a DAG edge. |\n135\t| E003 → BRANCH-A/B-E005, E005, BRANCH-A/B-E006 | Rule 9 | If license scanning fails, dependencies change and affect implementation approach. |\n136\t| E001 → BRANCH-A/B-E005, BRANCH-A/B-E006, E006 | Rule 3 | Topology outcome rewrites downstream deployment/enablement/Dashboard-linking scope; true gates recorded via `gated_by` + `gate_failure_impact`. |\n137\t| BRANCH-A-E005 → BRANCH-A-E006 (and B equivalent) | Rules 12/13 | Platform Operator enablement builds against the deployment artifacts (CRDs/manifests) produced by the topology-specific productization epic. |\n138\t| No edge from image build/konflux to Platform Operator enablement | Rule 13 | The Feast image digest consumed by operator enablement is a configuration reference — an AC (\"pinned image digest available\"), not a dependency. |\n139\t| E001 ∥ E002 ∥ E003 | Rules 14/15 | Investigation and onboarding work are independent; all three are DAG roots. |\n140\t| E005 (Notebooks repo) ∥ branch deployment epics (Feast repo) | Rule 14 | Different repos, no shared build artifacts; SDK preinstall is topology-independent. |\n141\t| E006 → E007, all implementations → E007 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by all Implementation epics; always last. |\n142\t| No priority push from E007 | Step 4 exception | docs-authoring priority derived from strategy `priority: Major` → P1, exempt from inheritance. |\n143\t\n144\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n145\t\n146\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n147\t|---|---|---|\n148\t| HLR-1 (operator enablement + productized images) | P0 | E001 (gate), E002, E003, E004, BRANCH-A-E005 + BRANCH-A-E006 or BRANCH-B-E005 + BRANCH-B-E006 |\n149\t| HLR-2 (Feast SDK in workbench image) | P1 | E005 (enabled by E003) |\n150\t| HLR-3 (Dashboard display + endpoint links) | P1 | E006 (gated by E001) |\n151\t| HLR-4 (product documentation) | P2 | E007 |\n152\t\n153\tAll HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements. No priority inversions detected:\n154\tonboarding-chain epics inherit P0 because they transitively enable HLR-1.\n155\t\n156\t## Health Warnings\n157\t\n158\t1. **Missing strategy sections** — Impacted Teams, Dependencies table, Acceptance\n159\t   Criteria, and NFRs are absent; teams were inferred and epic acceptance criteria\n160\t   were derived from HLRs and the problem statement. A human should confirm team\n161\t   assignments, especially the owning team for the new Feature Store component.\n162\t2. **Architecture context coverage gap** — only Dashboard has an architecture\n163\t   context file. Platform Operator and Notebooks are treated as in-platform based\n164\t   on the strategy's own statements (\"like any other managed component\", \"supported\n165\t   workbench image\"); Feature Store is correctly treated as new (onboarding chain\n166\t   generated). No unsubstantiated architecture claims were found.\n167\t3. **HLR-3 presumes per-project endpoints** — \"links users to its endpoints per\n168\t   project\" fits the standalone-server topology naturally; under an operator-based\n169\t   topology the endpoint granularity must be confirmed. The Dashboard epic is gated\n170\t   on the topology investigation for this reason.\n171\t4. **docs-authoring priority exception applied** — E007 is P1 (strategy priority\n172\t   Major) although HLR-4 is P2, per the docs-authoring priority rule.\n173\t\n174\t## Tiered Delivery\n175\t\n176\tNot applicable — no external dependency with uncertain timing. Feast is open source\n177\tand already public; the only unknown (topology) is an internal decision modeled as\n178\tan Investigation with conditional branches.\n179\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a23a14d3f41af05e","agent_id":"a9477bc38c6b9e204","session_id":"385beecc-1fc6-46ba-a853-90e78b018c5f","uuid":"810514de-a796-4bd6-87e6-8a4bfbc72bee","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:17:48.563Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2e2263558fb7f3c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
