upling is correctly carried as Rule 25 \"build\npipeline green\" ACs in E004 and the branch E005 epics. The Feast image digest\nconsumed by the branch enablement epics is correctly treated as a configuration\nreference (AC), not a dependency edge; the branch E005→E006 edge is justified by\nthe CRD/manifest artifact dependency, not the digest. Branch files all set both\n`branch` (matching filename) and `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001`. No main-plan\nepic lists a branch epic in its dependencies. Critical path length 3 is\nconsistent with the summary claim and reasonable for strategy size. Rule 11\nedges into E007 are valid and correctly do not trigger priority inheritance.\n\nMinor observations (not score-affecting):\n- E007's enablement and getting-started content describes work performed in the\n  branch epics; since main-plan epics cannot depend on branch nodes, the linkage\n  is implicit (via E006, which is gated by E001, plus the technical-review AC).\n  This is the rule-compliant structure, but the information flow is implicit.\n- E005's verification AC (\"retrieve features against a deployed Feature Store\n  endpoint... against an available deployment at execution time\") presumes a\n  deployment that no main-plan predecessor produces; E005 is deliberately\n  parallel to the branch deployment epics. The wording hedges this, but the\n  verification dependency is never made explicit.\n\n### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n\nEvery epic has a single component/team tuple, and all component names match the\ncanonical component list (Feature Store, Notebooks, Dashboard, Platform\nOperator, Documentation). No epic bundles multiple teams. No scope duplication:\nthe branch A/B E005 epics are mutually exclusive by design, the branch E005/E006\npairs split producer/consumer along the component boundary, and E005 (workbench\nSDK) shares no work product with the branch deployment epics. Work-product types\nare not mixed — the docs-authoring epic (E007) is separate from all code\nimplementation epics. No epic shows signs of exceeding ~2 weeks of work.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n\nE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome selects which conditional branch\nexists and rewrites the Dashboard linking scope, so it changes downstream\nstructure. All Implementation epics produce concrete artifacts (repository,\nscan report, pipeline, image, Dashboard feature, deployment artifacts,\nenablement, docs). Gating metadata is correct: E006 and all four branch epics\nhave `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001` with `gate_failure_impact` populated\n(`action` + `fallback_approach`), and every `gated_by` target appears in that\nepic's direct `dependencies`. No epic lists an Investigation dependency without\n`gated_by`. The branch epics' `action: remove` semantics correctly model\nconditional existence.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n\nType-appropriate signal fields are used throughout: E001 carries\n`investigation_signals` (5-signal rubric) with `ai_signals: null`; all ten\nImplementation epics carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric) with\n`investigation_signals: null`. Signal values are consistent with the rubric and\nstrategy content: E006's `open_questions: -1` correctly reflects the unresolved\nendpoint granularity until the E001 gate resolves; BRANCH-A-E005's\n`external_dependency: -1` correctly reflects uncontrolled upstream operator\ngaps; E001's investigation signals match the rubric conditions (concrete\nenumerable question, public upstream sources, pip-runnable Feast, peripheral\ncluster/stakeholder dependence). E006's `architecture_claims: 1` is justified —\nthe Dashboard architecture context file exists and substantiates the strategy's\nclaims. AI signal rationale files exist for all 11 epics and their values match\nthe frontmatter. (Arithmetic/thresholds not checked — computed by pipeline.)\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n\nEvery epic has testable acceptance criteria derived from the strategy. All\nrule-mandated ACs are present wherever applicable: the Konflux \"build pipeline\ngreen\" AC in E004 and in both branch E005 epics (Rule 25); the Platform\nOperator build-pipeline-green AC in both branch E006 epics; enable/disable\nrollback-path ACs in both branch E006 epics (disable cleanly removes the\ndeployment); technical-review and published-through-process ACs in E007\n(docs-authoring). No epic body references sibling epics by bare draft ID — all\ncross-references use full epic IDs in frontmatter only, and body text refers to\nwork descriptively.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n\nAll strategy scope is covered: managed-component enablement with productized\nimages (HLR-1 via onboarding chain + branches), SDK-preinstalled workbench\nimage (HLR-2 via E005), Dashboard enabled-component display with per-project\nendpoint links (HLR-3 via E006), and enablement/getting-started/limits\ndocumentation (HLR-4 via E007). The out-of-scope boundaries are carried\nforward, not dropped: link-out-only in E006's scope, customer-bring-your-own\noffline-store in BRANCH-B-E005's AC and E007's limits topic. The strategy's\nsingle open question is modeled as Investigation E001 with both bounded\noutcomes covered by conditional branches A and B — exactly the two topologies\nthe strategy names. The strategy has no Prerequisites & Process Gates section,\nbut HLR-4 explicitly requires documentation and the docs-authoring epic E007 is\npresent. Missing strategy sections (Impacted Teams, Dependencies, ACs, NFRs)\nare surfaced as health warnings with inferred-team caveats rather than silently\ndropped.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41520,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-950f2e80ac0a51e4","agent_id":"a3e67ab0e93da2a1d","session_id":"385beecc-1fc6-46ba-a853-90e78b018c5f","uuid":"ae9fe7bd-cf34-4395-9c6e-88a1f6b47d82","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:26:58.675Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"